<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/17th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ottoman–Safavid War (1623–1639)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1623–1639</span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-safavid-wars">Ottoman–Safavid wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ottoman–Safavid War of 1623–1639 was the last major war between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a> and Safavid <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>. It began when <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbas-i-of-persia">Shah Abbas I</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baghdad">Baghdad</a> in 1624; the Ottomans failed for years to retake it, until <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sultan">Sultan</a> Murad IV recaptured the city in 1638. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-zuhab">Treaty of Zuhab</a> (1639) left <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a> to the Ottomans and most of the southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> to Iran, roughly fixing the frontier later followed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iraq">Iraq</a> with Iran.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ottoman-safavid-war-1623-1639.jpg" alt="Ottoman–Safavid War (1623–1639)" width="320" height="222" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 2.5 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Map_Safavid_persia.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
